statement:
Let $\mathcal P$ be a property of morphisms of schemes [def-pc-scheme] such that
(1) $\mathcal P$ is stable under base change: if $Y\to V$ has $\mathcal P$ and $V'\to V$ is any morphism of schemes, then the projection $Y\times_VV'\to V'$ [def-pc-fibre-product] has $\mathcal P$;
(2) if $m\ge0$ and $h_j:Y_j\to V_j$ ($j=1,\dots,m$) are morphisms with $\mathcal P$, then the induced morphism $\coprod_jY_j\to\coprod_jV_j$ of coproducts of schemes [lem-weil-pbc-scheme-coproduct-family] has $\mathcal P$;
(3) for every flat [def-weil-flat-morphism] surjective [def-weil-surjective-morphism] morphism $X\to S$ of affine schemes and every descent datum $(V,\varphi)$ on a scheme $V$ over $X/S$ [def-pd-descent-datum] such that $V\to X$ has $\mathcal P$, the descent datum is effective in the sense of [def-pd-descent-datum].
Then for every morphism of schemes $f:X\to S$ such that the one-member family $\{f:X\to S\}$ is an fpqc covering of $S$ [def-weil-pbc-fpqc-covering], and every descent datum $\varphi:\mathrm{pr}_0^*V\to\mathrm{pr}_1^*V$ on a scheme $V$ over $X/S$ [def-pd-descent-datum] (with $\mathrm{pr}_0,\mathrm{pr}_1:X\times_SX\to X$ the projections) such that $V\to X$ has $\mathcal P$, the descent datum is effective: there are a scheme $U$ with a morphism $U\to S$ and an isomorphism $\psi:U\times_SX\to V$ of schemes over $X$ such that $\varphi\circ\mathrm{pr}_0^*\psi=\mathrm{pr}_1^*\psi\circ\mathrm{can}_U$, where $\mathrm{can}_U:\mathrm{pr}_0^*(U\times_SX)\to\mathrm{pr}_1^*(U\times_SX)$ is the composite of the canonical isomorphisms of both sides with $U\times_S(X\times_SX)$.
